From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 04:26:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk: NVK_DISPATCH_CAPTURE captures draws too

A hash in NVK_DISPATCH_CAPTURE that matches the bound fragment shader
(its DXIL source hash or its 8-digit code hash) captures a vkCmdDraw,
vkCmdDrawIndexed or one of their indirect and indirect-count forms with
it (an indirect draw with its records and count as they were when it
ran, and the whole bound index buffer): both shaders' SPIR-V, their
descriptors and root buffers, the color, depth and stencil attachments'
contents, the indices the draw reads and the vertex buffers its
attributes read (as bound, up to 256 MiB each), and the pipeline state
(topology, rasterization, depth bias, viewport, scissor, render area,
depth/stencil and blend state, attachment formats, vertex input), in the
same capture format with "kind": "draw" and vs.spv.  dispatch-replay
replays it as that draw.

The common runtime gets vk_device::graphics_spirv_hook, called with the
SPIR-V of each graphics shader of a new pipeline, and graphics shaders
get their SPIR-V source hash.  While the hook is installed, graphics
stages are precompiled from their SPIR-V, not taken from the pipeline
cache (a cached precompiled shader has no SPIR-V).  NVK notes the bound vertex and
index buffers for this whatever the state tracking.  A listed fragment shader bound
for vkCmdExecuteGeneratedCommandsEXT is logged, not captured.  Draws with
tessellation, geometry or mesh shaders, multisampling or multiview are
logged, not captured.

A capture whose staging with the outputs (NVK_DISPATCH_CAPTURE_POST)
cannot be mapped is made without the outputs.
